{
  "cell": "opamp_comp",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py (issue #167). See",
    "layout/opamp_comp/README.md for the floorplan, conventions and results.",
    "",
    "SCOPE: the Miller compensation network of design/netlist/opamp_core.spice,",
    "XRz (res_high_po_1p41, L=9.765, model-default W=1.41) in series with XCc",
    "(cap_mim_m3_1, W=L=15.62) at node cz: d2 -XRz- cz -XCc- out, XRz substrate",
    "on vss. Passive sub-block only; NOT the full core.",
    "",
    "BLOCKS: rz = klt res_array (num=1, dummy=0, flavor high), cc = klt",
    "cap_array (num=1, 15.62 x 15.62 top plate), tap = klt guard_ring p-tap ring",
    "(add_well=false) giving the resistor substrate a vss contact, tap_masks =",
    "klt-draw psdm 94/20 over the ring (the klt generators do not draw sky130",
    "implants; klayout-tools#2934). The ring is a sibling of Rz, not a guard",
    "ring around it: the extractor ties the resistor body to the substrate net,",
    "which the ring then names vss.",
    "",
    "PINS: d2 (li1, west), out (met3 = cap bottom plate, west), cz (met4 = cap",
    "top plate, observation pin: the LVS flow has no internal-only nets so the",
    "shared node is exposed), vss (li1, east of the ring).",
    "cz plates: cz is the top (capm / met4) plate, out the bottom (met3) plate;",
    "klt LVS treats the plates as interchangeable, so this is a floorplan choice.",
    "",
    "rz_masks: RPM 86/20, PSDM 94/20 and NPC 95/20 over the whole poly outline.",
    "res_array draws RPM/PSDM over the body only and no NPC; without these the",
    "PDK Magic sees no resistor (klayout-tools#3077).",
    "rz x = 2.005: Magic extracts the 9.765 um body only when its edges sit at a",
    "5 nm offset from its 10 nm input scale. pin_cz x = 20.0 keeps the cz",
    "backbone centre line (midway between R0_B and the stub) on the 0.005 grid.",
    "lvs.layout_input = gds: the pre-extracted netlist form cannot read the",
    "resistor (klayout-tools#3078)."
  ],
